// SIGNALS admits exactly five values -- Rule 118's family one:
// success, warning, danger, info, muted.
//
// 'critical' is a real word in this language, but it belongs to TONE, which is
// the register the system SPEAKS in. SIGNALS says what a value MEANS about a
// record. Two strata, two closed vocabularies, and each refuses the other's --
// which is the point: borrowing across them is exactly how one subject ends up
// with two vocabularies that drift.
//
// Expected: UNKNOWN_SIGNAL

DEFINE SCREEN overdue_invoices (
  SATISFIES [SCAN, COMPARE, LOCATE],
  SIGNALS [danger, critical]
)
